# @mirror/spec/system — the grammar species-decl for `system @NAME
# { s1..s5 + feedback_loops + kintsugi_tooling }` block at .spec-
# file altitude; the compile-altitude landing of Beer's VSM per
# Alex Round-3 spawn brief.
#
# Species under @mirror/spec (sibling to the existing `project(name)
# -> prism` grammar at :52). Landed 2026-07-20 by Mara Round-3 per
# Alex Round-3 spawn brief §Tier 1.2. Alias-shim from `project` per
# two-tick discipline (§Migration below).
#
# === The species altitude ===
#
# `mirror.spec` grammar altitude. Per Alex Round-3 spawn brief
# verbatim:
#
#   > "Mirror as the formalization of Beer's VSM at compiler altitude
#   >  producing geometric supervisor systems for the Erlang VM."
#
# @mirror/spec/system IS the compile-altitude grammar species at
# which Beer's VSM lands as a `system @NAME { s1..s5 + feedback_loops
# + kintsugi_tooling }` block. The block reads as literal English:
#
#   system @my_project {
#     s1 { ... operations ... }
#     s2 { ... coordination ... }
#     s3 { ... audit ... }
#     s4 { ... intelligence ... }
#     s5 { ... identity ... }
#     feedback_loops { ... }
#     kintsugi_tooling { ... }
#   }
#
# The reader who has been reading Beer for 50 years already knows
# how to read this. That's the "sharp AND delightfully boring"
# discipline in force: Beer's actual word, Beer's actual structure,
# compile-verifiable via witnessed-property predicates.
#
# === Alias-shim from `project` per two-tick discipline ===
#
# Per Alex Round-3 spawn brief §Tier 1.2: "Alias-shim from `project`
# per two-tick discipline. ~500-800 LOC."
#
# The current mirror.spec grammar at `shards/mirror/spec.mirror` :52
# declares:
#
#   project(name) -> prism { \ }
#
# This species adds the sibling `system(name) -> prism` grammar; the
# `project` grammar remains operational as an ALIAS-SHIM for one
# release cycle per two-tick discipline (per [[feedback-legibility-
# over-foundation-when-collapsing]]).
#
# Two-tick migration:
#
#   TICK 1 (this tick):
#     - Land `system(name) -> prism` grammar species
#     - Keep `project(name) -> prism` operational (unchanged surface)
#     - Add `system` keyword to @mirror/spec grammar keywords
#     - Preserve consumer stability (existing mirror.spec files
#       using `project` continue to work)
#
#   TICK 2 (next release cycle):
#     - Deprecate `project` grammar (deprecation warning)
#     - Update mirror.spec (the dogfood) to use `system @mirror.spec`
#     - Update downstream consumer specs
#     - Retire `project` grammar (following release cycle)
#
# The dogfood update in mirror.spec at compile-altitude altitude is
# forward-promised for TICK 2; NOT this tick per two-tick discipline
# (preserve consumer stability).
#
# === Composition-primitive naming ===
#
# Per feedback_composition_primitive_naming_convention:
#
#   system(name) -> prism
#
# Reads: given a name, produces a prism (the substrate manifold
# @mirror/mosaic.focus reads to produce the build manifold).
#
# === The seven sub-directives ===
#
# Per Round-3 brief §Tier 1.2 + Beer 1972-1984 VSM structure, the
# `system @NAME { ... }` block admits SEVEN sub-directives:
#
#   s1 { ... }                — S1 operations block (workers +
#                                variety-producers; each S1 is
#                                itself a viable system per Beer
#                                1972 ch.10 recursive viability)
#   s2 { ... }                — S2 coordination block (anti-
#                                oscillation between S1s; shared
#                                protocol per @dance ensemble
#                                altitude)
#   s3 { ... }                — S3 audit / management block
#                                (restart_strategy at supervision
#                                altitude per @spectral/supervisor)
#   s4 { ... }                — S4 intelligence / strategy block
#                                (@spectral/db psychohistory carrier
#                                altitude)
#   s5 { ... }                — S5 identity / policy block (Pack S5
#                                or subject-identity per viable.
#                                identity carrier)
#   feedback_loops { ... }    — the feedback-loop declarations
#                                (algedonic bypass channel per Beer
#                                1979 ch.6; adjacent-level feedback
#                                per Baez-Schreiber connection
#                                compatibility)
#   kintsugi_tooling { ... }  — the tooling declarations at the
#                                system's kintsugi discipline
#                                altitude (@kintsugi + @kintsugi/
#                                roomba + @kintsugi/fracture
#                                composition; how the system heals
#                                its own perturbations)
#
# Each sub-directive is a typed lambda per @mirror/spec discipline;
# the obligation blocks (\) discharge at mosaic.focus consumer
# altitude.
#
# === Substrate-already-had-the-word audit ===
#
# 1. **No prior `shards/mirror/spec/system.mirror`** — clean naming
#    space (the directory `shards/mirror/spec/` currently contains
#    only `keywords.mirror`).
# 2. **`shards/mirror/spec.mirror`** — reviewed. Family-root prism +
#    `project(name) -> prism` grammar at :52. @mirror/spec/system is
#    the SIBLING grammar per two-tick alias-shim discipline;
#    substrate consumers migrate incrementally. No conflict; the
#    two grammars coexist during migration cycle.
# 3. **`shards/mirror/spec/keywords.mirror`** — reviewed. Companion
#    keyword bindings for the tokenizer's harvester; extended this
#    tick to add `system` keyword (per @mirror/spec/keywords
#    extension below OR sibling shard update).
# 4. **`shards/system.mirror`** — reviewed (this tick). @system
#    family-root marker; @mirror/spec/system inherits at species
#    altitude; the grammar species IS the compile-altitude form of
#    what the family-root NAMES.
# 5. **`shards/epistemologic/cybernetic/viable.mirror`** — reviewed.
#    Property-altitude VSM carriers. @mirror/spec/system's SEVEN
#    sub-directives correspond to viable.mirror's carriers + Beer
#    1979 ch.6 algedonic + kintsugi discipline. Sibling altitudes;
#    grammar species carries the syntax, viable carries the
#    semantics.
# 6. **`shards/beam/system.mirror`** (this tick) — reviewed. Sibling
#    species-under-@system at BEAM runtime altitude; @mirror/spec/
#    system at compile-altitude altitude. Two altitudes; both are
#    species of @system.
#
# === Substrate authority chain ===
#
# - **Alex Round-3 spawn brief** (verbatim; §Tier 1.2): "shards/
#   mirror/spec/system.mirror — grammar species-decl for `system
#   @NAME { ... }` block with S1-S5 sub-directives. Composition-
#   primitive naming per feedback_composition_primitive_naming_
#   convention. Alias-shim from `project` per two-tick discipline.
#   ~500-800 LOC."
# - **`shards/system.mirror`** (this tick) — the family-root marker
#   this species is under.
# - **`shards/mirror/spec.mirror`** — the family-root prism this
#   species is a sibling grammar within.
# - **Beer 1972/1979/1984** — the VSM structure the SEVEN sub-
#   directives correspond to.
# - **Alex Round-3 spawn brief §The one-sentence positioning** —
#   the compile-altitude landing this grammar makes verbatim.
#
# === The system_spec carrier ===
#
# The typed carrier for a `system @NAME { ... }` block. Composes the
# seven sub-directives as typed fields.
#
#   name              — the block's name (per `system @NAME`
#                        header; identity contract).
#   s1_operations     — the S1 sub-directive contents (per BEAM
#                        gen_prism worker altitude).
#   s2_coordination   — the S2 sub-directive contents (per @dance
#                        ensemble altitude).
#   s3_audit          — the S3 sub-directive contents (per
#                        @spectral/supervisor restart_strategy).
#   s4_intelligence   — the S4 sub-directive contents (per
#                        @spectral/db psychohistory).
#   s5_identity       — the S5 sub-directive contents (per viable.
#                        identity + @pack.peer).
#   feedback_loops    — the feedback-loop declarations (per Beer
#                        1979 ch.6 algedonic + Baez-Schreiber
#                        connection compatibility).
#   kintsugi_tooling  — the kintsugi tooling declarations (per
#                        @kintsugi discipline).
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the eight-field record.
type system_spec = {
  name:             str,
  s1_operations:    ref,
  s2_coordination:  ref,
  s3_audit:         ref,
  s4_intelligence:  ref,
  s5_identity:      identity,
  feedback_loops:   ref,
  kintsugi_tooling: ref,
}

# === system — the top-level keyword grammar ===
#
# Per Alex Round-3 spawn brief §Tier 1.2 verbatim. Reads:
#
#   system @my_project { s1 {...} s2 {...} s3 {...} s4 {...}
#                         s5 {...} feedback_loops {...}
#                         kintsugi_tooling {...} }
#
# The grammar consumer is @mirror/mosaic.focus (per @mirror/spec's
# consumer discipline). The obligation block (\) discharges when
# mosaic.focus walks the manifold.
#
# Alias-shim discipline: `project(name) -> prism` remains operational
# at `shards/mirror/spec.mirror` :52; both grammars coexist during
# migration cycle. TICK 2 (forward-promised) deprecates `project`
# and updates the dogfood mirror.spec to use `system`.
system(name) -> prism { \ }

# === the seven sub-directives inside a `system` block ===
#
# Each is a typed lambda (substrate's action form, per @mirror/spec
# discipline); the obligation block (\) is discharged by mosaic.focus
# when it walks the manifold.

# s1 { ... }
#
# S1 operations block. Declares the variety-producers at BEAM/process
# altitude (workers + gen_prism instances per @spectral/gen_prism).
# Each S1 is itself a viable system per Beer 1972 ch.10 recursive
# viability; the sub-directive body admits nested `system @X { ... }`
# declarations at S1 altitude for recursion.
s1(operations: ref) -> prism { \ }

# s2 { ... }
#
# S2 coordination block. Declares the anti-oscillation protocol
# between S1s (per @dance ensemble altitude; Kuramoto phase-lock
# connection 1-form at level k+1). Forward-promised: @dance ensemble
# carrier per Mara Round-1 landings.
s2(coordination: ref) -> prism { \ }

# s3 { ... }
#
# S3 audit / management block. Declares the restart_strategy
# discipline at supervision altitude (per @spectral/supervisor +
# restart_intensity + connection at supervision-connection altitude
# per beam-runtime.md §5).
s3(audit: ref) -> prism { \ }

# s4 { ... }
#
# S4 intelligence / strategy block. Declares the psychohistory
# carrier at @spectral/db altitude (per @resonance inter-peer coupling
# discipline).
s4(intelligence: ref) -> prism { \ }

# s5 { ... }
#
# S5 identity / policy block. Declares the identity carrier at Pack
# S5 altitude (per viable.identity + @pack.peer + @subject
# discipline; the peer/pack whose identity IS the system's identity-
# policy).
s5(identity: identity) -> prism { \ }

# feedback_loops { ... }
#
# Declares the feedback-loop topology at Beer 1979 ch.6 algedonic
# altitude + Baez-Schreiber connection-compatibility altitude. Names
# the S1→S5 emergency-bypass channel + adjacent-level feedback per
# viable.mirror algedonic_signal carrier.
feedback_loops(loops: ref) -> prism { \ }

# kintsugi_tooling { ... }
#
# Declares the kintsugi discipline for the system: how the system
# heals its own perturbations via @kintsugi + @kintsugi/roomba +
# @kintsugi/fracture composition. Sub-directives inside admit the
# @kintsugi/consent + @kintsugi/mosaic + @kintsugi/oscillate
# discipline references.
kintsugi_tooling(tooling: ref) -> prism { \ }

# === system_spec_well_formed — bilateral predicate ===
#
# Discharges Pass iff:
#   - name is non-empty
#   - all five S1-S5 sub-directive references are non-null (Beer
#     1972-1984 requires all five VSM subsystems present)
#   - feedback_loops declares at minimum the algedonic S1→S5 bypass
#     channel per Beer 1979 ch.6
#   - kintsugi_tooling references at minimum the @kintsugi family-
#     root discipline
#   - s5_identity discharges viable.viable_well_formed at the
#     species boundary
#
# Rice-safe bound: reads only byte-visible state (ref-non-null,
# string-emptiness, viable_well_formed Rice-safe discharge).
#
# Sentinel: `mirror-spec-system=well-formed-vsm-seven-directive-block`.
bilateral system_spec_well_formed {
  sentinel "mirror-spec-system=well-formed-vsm-seven-directive-block"
  arity 1
}
system_spec_well_formed(s: system_spec) -> verdict { \ }

